  "question": {
    "text": "<strong>Paragraph:</strong>\nThe nuclear charge $(\\mathrm{Ze})$ is non-uniformly distributed within a nucleus of radius $R$. The charge density $\\rho(r)$ [charge per unit volume] is dependent only on the radial distance $r$ from the centre of the nucleus as shown in figure. The electric field is only along the radial direction.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/jlFKxAkJt_03DKXWqhIFlKSRLGpw3OZjlz0a8gNGa4M.original.fullsize.png\"><br><strong>Question:</strong>\nFor $a=0$, the value of $d$ (maximum value of $\\rho$ as shown in the figure) is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Lvmb2",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{3 Z e}{4 \\pi R^3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "hxgpR",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{3 Z e}{\\pi R^3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "xnGod",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{4 Z e}{3 \\pi R^3}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "aRXGM",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{Z e}{3 \\pi R^3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For $a=0$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\rho(r)=\\left(-\\frac{d}{R} \\cdot r+d\\right) \\\\\n& \\text { Now } \\int_0^R\\left(4 \\pi r^2\\right)\\left(d-\\frac{d}{R} r\\right) d r=\\text { net charge }=Z e\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nSolving this equation, we get $d=\\frac{3 Z e}{\\pi R^3}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/LyvPQp1nkAouhegtu45_JVyeZAs0gj3wpNxj90T5ADo.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
